<Doc
	title="Privacy Policy | Take Flight"
	description="Privacy policy for Take Flight. No personal data is collected or stored by the developer."
	eyebrow="Take Flight"
	heading="Privacy Policy"
	intro="Take Flight is built with your privacy in mind. The developer does not collect or store any personal data."
	footnote="Effective date: March 2026 · Last updated: March 2026"
>
	<section>
		<h2>No Data Collected by the Developer</h2>
		<p>
			Take Flight does not collect, transmit, store, or share any personal data with the developer.
			There are no user accounts, no sign-in requirements, and no analytics or tracking of any kind.
			The app's privacy label reflects this: no data types are collected or linked to your identity
			by the developer.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Game Center</h2>
		<p>
			Take Flight integrates Apple Game Center for leaderboards and achievements. When you use Game
			Center features, Apple collects and manages your Game Center profile, scores, and achievement
			data in accordance with <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>. The developer has no access to your
			Game Center data beyond what Apple surfaces through public leaderboard APIs.
		</p>
		<p>
			Game Center participation is optional. You can decline Game Center sign-in when prompted, or
			sign out in iOS Settings at any time.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Local Storage & Data Retention</h2>
		<p>
			Take Flight stores game progress, high scores, and settings locally on your device using
			SwiftData and standard iOS storage mechanisms. Nothing is synced to external servers by the
			developer. Because no data is collected by the app itself, there is no server-side retention
			period.
		</p>
		<p>
			All locally stored content is retained on your device until you delete it or uninstall Take
			Flight. Uninstalling the app permanently removes all associated local data.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>App Permissions</h2>
		<p>Take Flight may request the following iOS permission:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Game Center</strong> - used for leaderboards and achievements. Managed entirely by
				Apple.
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			Permissions are requested only when you initiate the relevant action. You can revoke Game
			Center access at any time in iOS Settings.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>No Third-Party SDKs</h2>
		<p>
			Take Flight contains no third-party analytics, advertising, crash reporting, or tracking
			frameworks. There are no external dependencies beyond Apple's own frameworks (SpriteKit,
			SwiftUI, SwiftData, Game Center, AVFoundation) that could introduce data collection or
			sharing by a third party.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Deleting Your Data</h2>
		<p>
			Because all game data is stored locally on your device, you are always in full control of it.
			To remove all data associated with Take Flight, uninstall the app from your device. This
			permanently deletes all locally stored content.
		</p>
		<p>
			For Game Center data (scores, achievements), manage or delete your Game Center profile
			through Apple's Settings or by contacting Apple directly.
		</p>
		<p>
			There is no developer-side account to close and no server-side data to request deletion of -
			none exists.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Your Rights</h2>
		<p>
			Depending on where you live, you may have rights regarding your personal data under
			applicable law (including the EU General Data Protection Regulation, UK GDPR, and California
			Consumer Privacy Act). Because Take Flight does not collect, process, or store any personal
			data on external systems, there is no personal data held by the developer to access, correct,
			export, or erase.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you have any questions or wish to exercise any rights, you can contact the developer
			directly at <a href="mailto:jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com">jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com</a>.
		</p>
		<p><strong>Data controller:</strong> Jaiden Henley - jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			Take Flight is not directed at children under the age of 13 (or under 16 in applicable EU
			member states). The app does not knowingly collect any personal information from children.
			Because no data is collected from any user, no data is collected from minors.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Apple's Role</h2>
		<p>
			Take Flight is distributed through Apple TestFlight and the Apple App Store. Apple may
			collect certain device and transaction information as part of operating the App Store,
			TestFlight, and iOS platform. This collection is governed by <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>, not this policy. The Take Flight developer has no access to any
			data Apple collects.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you use iCloud Backup, iOS will include your locally stored Take Flight data in that
			backup. This is managed entirely by Apple and iOS - the developer has no access to backed-up
			content.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
		<p>
			If this policy is updated, the revised version will be posted at this URL with an updated
			date. Continued use of the app after any change constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section>
		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			For any questions about this privacy policy, contact:
			<a href="mailto:jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com">jaidenhenleydev@gmail.com</a>
		</p>
	</section>
</Doc>
